{
  "about": "Ticket proposal result (relay-api.md 'Ticket proposal result'). valid / invalid: texts that pass / fail message.schema.json. body.text is REQUIRED and is the canonical line derived from the result: made -> 'Ticket made: <key>', refused -> \"Couldn't make the ticket\", decided -> 'Already decided' or, with a key, 'Ticket made: <key>'. New phones hide the bubble and fold the result into the card by reply_to; old phones show the plain line. relay: what the relay answers (expect = HTTP status; 200 = identical duplicate) given state: the proposal is m_pr00000000000001 (a make_ticket question ws_pilatus001 sent to phones), answered_by = phones whose answer for it the relay stored, results = proposal_result messages already stored for it; m_qq00000000000001 is an ordinary question and m_tt00000000000001 a text of ws_pilatus001, m_pr0000other00001 a proposal of ws_other00001. A relay implementation replays every entry against the relay itself, not only the schema. cases: what the workspace does after a phone answer (authorised = a paired phone answered, not group-routed; state open|made|gone|answered_make|answered_not_now|result_recorded; send = the proposal_result body or null; to = phones or the answering ph_; got_it_ack = whether the ordinary Got it ack is sent). phone: the card a phone shows after the events (a result event applies only to the proposal the phone asked about; made is final for one reply_to). answered_by (relay state) = the phone whose answer for the proposal the relay stored: the relay keeps only the FIRST answer per question (a second one, from any phone, is 409 already_answered on POST /v1/phone/answer), so only that phone gets refused/decided. A case with skipped: true sends nothing because a keyed decided would repeat the made broadcast that phone already got. Exact bytes of body.text: ASCII apostrophe U+0027 in Couldn't, no trailing period, one ASCII space after the colon.",
  "phone_ids": {
    "ph_iphone0001": "iPhone",
    "ph_iphone0002": "iPad"
  },
